Red Sparrow is a 2018 American spy thriller film directed by Francis Lawrence and written by
Justin Haythe, based on the 2013 novel of the same name by Jason Matthews.

14
01:29:05,454 --> 01:29:11,454
The film stars Jennifer Lawrence, Joel Edgerton, Matthias Schoenaerts, Charlotte
Rampling, Mary-Louise Parker, Jeremy Irons, and Ciarán Hinds.

15
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
It tells the story of a former-ballerina-turned-Russian intelligence officer, who is sent to
make contact with a CIA officer in the hope of discovering the identity of a mole.

16
01:41:49,090 --> 01:41:55,090
Matthews, a former member of the CIA, advised the
production on the depiction of spying.

17
01:48:10,909 --> 01:48:16,909
Based on historic Soviet sexpionage and contemporary Russian use of
kompromat, filming took place in Hungary, Slovakia and Austria.

18
01:54:32,727 --> 01:54:38,727
Red Sparrow premiered at the Newseum in Washington, D.C., on February 15,
2018, and was released in the United States on March 2, 2018.

19
